this project is a distillation of the various design decisions for soramech.
... that name could probably be improved.

anyway it's intended to be as minimal an implementation of the structure as
possible, or rather, a minimal default template that other use-cases can
build upon. It strips out the cross-language compatibility concern (which,
admittedly, was one of it's main benefits) and instead focuses on the
multi-threaded by default architecture support. It essentially becomes an
engine that other programs can be created with, rather than a swiss-army-tool
knife that has the capability to act as an arbitrary bridge for various
languages. If the user wants to call a specific function using soramech, they
can more easily do it by creating a custom box for the specific language in
question rather than depending on the architecture. An increase in focus
requires a subtraction of concern, and we are focusing on the platform rather
than the bridge.

